<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Document</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  body {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <img src="placeholder_seal.png" alt="Seal" style="width: 100px; height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 18pt; margin: 0;">DEPARTMENT OF THE TREASURY</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin: 2px 0;">INTERNAL REVENUE SERVICE</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin: 2px 0;">WASHINGTON, D.C. {{ current_year }}</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">{{ date_sent }}</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">CC:ITA:B04:</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Number: <span data-field="document_number">{{ document_number }}</span></p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Release Date: <span data-field="release_date">{{ release_date }}</span></p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">CONEX-{{ document_id }}</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">UIL: <span data-field="uil_number">{{ uil_number }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">The Honorable <span data-field="recipient_full_name">{{ recipient_full_name }}</span></p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">United States Senator</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">{{ recipient_street_address }}</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">{{ recipient_city_state_zip }}</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Attention:</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Dear Senator <span data-field="recipient_last_name">{{ recipient_last_name }}</span>:</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">I am responding to your inquiry dated {{ inquiry_date }}, on behalf of your constituent asked whether payment <span data-field="payment_description">{{ payment_description }}</span> received in a breach of contract lawsuit settlement is excludible from gross income under the Internal Revenue Code (the Code). <span data-field="explanation_summary">{{ explanation_summary }}</span></p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">I'm sorry to hear of the difficulty <span data-field="difficulty_description">{{ difficulty_description }}</span> experienced due to a breach of contract lawsuit.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">While I can provide certain general principles of the law, this information is intended for informational purposes only. It does not constitute a ruling.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">A private letter ruling interprets the tax laws and applies them to the taxpayer's specific set of facts. A taxpayer may request a private letter ruling by submitting a written request under the procedures described in Revenue Procedure {{ revenue_procedure_number }}, Section {{ section_number }}, {{ date_procedure }}.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Whether settlement proceeds are excludable from gross income as damages received on account of personal physical injuries or physical sickness is, in part, a factual</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: right; margin-bottom: 10px;">
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">CONEX-{{ document_id }}</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">2</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">In reaching this determination, courts generally look at the settlement agreement in light of all of the surrounding circumstances. A court may look at the allegations of the complaint to determine whether the claims to which the proceeds are allocated in the settlement agreement are claims for personal physical injuries or physical sickness. However, the mere mention of "personal physical injuries" in a complaint does not, by itself, serve to bring a recovery within the exclusion.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Section {{ section_number_61a }} of the Code defines gross income as all income from whatever source derived. Gross income means all undeniable accessions to wealth, clearly realized, over which the taxpayers have complete dominion, unless specifically excluded.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">{{ case_citation }}</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Section {{ section_number_104a2 }} of the Code excludes from gross income the amount of any damages (excluding punitive damages) received on account of personal physical injuries or physical sickness. However, damages received for emotional distress do not qualify for this exclusion, unless they are recovered because of a personal physical injury or physical sickness or are less than the amount paid for medical care due to the emotional distress.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">I hope this general information is helpful. If you have additional questions, you may contact me at</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Sincerely,</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">{{ signatory_name }}</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Branch Chief, Branch 4</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">(Income Tax & Accounting)</p>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>